# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mobile LAN-dev environment — loaded by `npm run build:mobile:lan`
# (`vite build --mode mobile`).
#
# This profile exists because of one fact: inside a packaged app, `localhost` is
# the PHONE, not the dev machine. Every host in env/.env.development points at
# loopback, so a native build made from it reaches nothing and every screen shows
# a network error that looks like a backend outage. The Flutter agent app hit the
# same wall and settled on an explicit dev-machine host; this mirrors that
# rather than inventing a second convention.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS A DEVELOPMENT PROFILE. The store build is `npm run build:mobile`,
# which uses env/.env.production. Nothing here reaches a release artifact.
#
# Vite loads `.env`, `.env.mobile` and `.env.mobile.local` for `--mode mobile`
# — NOT `.env.production`, so this file has to be self-contained.
#
# `import.meta.env.DEV` is still FALSE here: Vite sets NODE_ENV=production for
# every `vite build` regardless of `--mode`. So VITE_FORCE_MOBILE_AUTH is folded
# away and cannot be set from this file — which is correct, because a native
# build is already on the bearer transport via `isNative`.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── THE ONE LINE TO CHANGE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The dev machine's address as the PHONE can reach it. Every host below is built
# from it, so there is exactly one value to keep current — and `DEV_HOST` has no
# VITE_ prefix, so it configures the build without being exposed to the bundle.
# (Vite runs dotenv-expand over these files, which is what makes `${DEV_HOST}`
# resolve; `npm run build:mobile:lan` then inlines the expanded URLs.)
#
# Pick whichever is true when you build:
#
#   · SAME WI-FI as the dev machine → its LAN address. DIRECT connection,
#     sub-millisecond, no third party in the path. This is the default and the
#     one to prefer whenever it applies. `ipconfig` prints it; it comes from
#     DHCP, so it can change when the router hands out a new lease.
#
#   · PHONE ELSEWHERE (mobile data, another network) → the TAILSCALE address
#     100.124.149.1: (`tailscale ip -4`). Stable across networks, but see the
#     warning below before reaching for it.
#
# ⚠ THE TAILSCALE PATH IS CURRENTLY RELAYED, NOT DIRECT. `tailscale netcheck`
#   on this machine reports `UDP: false`, which means it cannot hole-punch and
#   every packet is relayed through a DERP server (nearest: Johannesburg,
#   ~215ms) over a throughput-capped TCP tunnel. That is what makes the app
#   "work sometimes and not others" on the tailnet host. It is a firewall
#   problem on the dev machine, not an app problem — allow Tailscale's inbound
#   UDP in Windows Defender Firewall and `netcheck` should report a real IPv4
#   address, at which point this host is as good as the LAN one.
DEV_HOST=192.168.1.102
# DEV_HOST=100.124.149.1:

# Two things still have to be true, and neither is about the address:
#   · the phone can actually route to it — same Wi-Fi for the LAN host, same
#     tailnet (`tailscale status` lists the other) for the Tailscale one;
#   · Windows Defender Firewall allows inbound 8022. The backend binds every
#     interface (`app.listen(PORT)` with no host), so the firewall is the usual
#     reason a correct address still times out.
#
# Override in env/.env.mobile.local (git-ignored) rather than editing here when
# the value is personal to your machine.

# wi-mall backend — all /api calls go here. Must end in /api.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://100.124.149.1:8022/api

# Base URL where uploaded files are served (defaults to the API origin /uploads).
# VITE_FILE_BASE_URL=

# App display name.
VITE_APP_NAME=Wi-Agency

# NOTE: no VITE_LOGIN_URL. Login is in-app from Phase 1 (src/pages/Login.tsx);
# the external redirect it configured no longer exists in the code.

# ─── Live tracking (geo-tracker, the separate Go WebSocket service) ────────────
# Same host. On native the socket authenticates with a bearer token via the
# `window.wiMallGetAccessToken` seam (Phase 4, P4.6) — not with a cookie, which
# is why VITE_GEO_TRACKER_TOKEN stays empty here.
VITE_GEO_TRACKER_WS_URL=ws://100.124.149.1:8090/ws/track
# VITE_GEO_TRACKER_URL=
VITE_GEO_TRACKER_TOKEN=

# ─── Live Tracking basemap (Leaflet) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset uses the built-in default (CARTO, keyless, light + dark). Tiles come from
# the public internet, so they work on a device even when the LAN backend does
# not — a map that renders while the data does not means the API host is wrong,
# not the network.
# VITE_MAP_TILE_URL=
# VITE_MAP_TILE_URL_DARK=
# VITE_MAP_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=

# ─── Push notifications ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately absent. The VITE_FIREBASE_* values drive the *web push* provider
# in src/lib/push.ts, which P2.6 disables on native — a service worker in a
# WebView registers happily and never receives anything. Native push arrives in
# Phase 4 (P4.1) and is configured by android/app/google-services.json from the
# MESSAGING Firebase project, not by any variable in this file.

# ─── Payments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, deliberately. Billing is read-only on mobile
# (D4 / Phase 5): plan upgrades and top-ups route to the web dashboard, so no
# publishable key is needed and shipping one would only make the unreachable path
# look reachable.
#
# Where those two route TO. The production default (https://agency.wi-mall.com)
# is a live site with a different backend than the dev one this build talks to,
# so on-device the notice would send you somewhere your test agency does not
# exist. Point it at the dev server on the same machine — same host as the API
# above, Vite's port.
#
# NB two things this needs that the API does not: `npm run dev` binds loopback
# only, so start it with `npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0`; and the page it opens
# is a browser tab whose ORIGIN is http://<DEV_HOST>:5174, which the backend's
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS must name or its API calls are refused. The notice is the only
# thing that opens it; nothing else in the app breaks without it.
VITE_WEB_DASHBOARD_URL=http://100.124.149.1:5174
